From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kreijstal <elektrischrainbow@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 17:03:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mingw: export the AOTI / stable ABI C shim from torch_cpu

With GCC, AOTI_TORCH_EXPORT is a visibility attribute, which exports
nothing from a PE DLL. libtorch_cpu.dll then does not export the
aoti_torch_* / torch_* C shim of the stable ABI, and extensions built on
it (torchvision >= 0.29, STABLE_TORCH_LIBRARY) fail to link. On MinGW,
dllexport them while building torch_cpu, which defines all of them, and
dllimport them elsewhere, as MSVC builds do.
---
 torch/csrc/inductor/aoti_torch/c/macros.h | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/torch/csrc/inductor/aoti_torch/c/macros.h b/torch/csrc/inductor/aoti_torch/c/macros.h
index e49cd39..ee6933a 100644
--- a/torch/csrc/inductor/aoti_torch/c/macros.h
+++ b/torch/csrc/inductor/aoti_torch/c/macros.h
@@ -3,8 +3,17 @@
 
 #include <stddef.h>
 #include <stdint.h>
-#ifdef __GNUC__
+#if defined(__GNUC__) && !defined(_WIN32)
 #define AOTI_TORCH_EXPORT __attribute__((__visibility__("default")))
+#elif defined(__GNUC__) // MinGW
+// Visibility attributes export nothing from a PE DLL, so libtorch_cpu would
+// not export the AOTI / stable ABI C shim. CMake defines torch_cpu_EXPORTS
+// for the sources of torch_cpu, which defines all of these functions.
+#if defined(EXPORT_AOTI_FUNCTIONS) || defined(torch_cpu_EXPORTS)
+#define AOTI_TORCH_EXPORT __declspec(dllexport)
+#else
+#define AOTI_TORCH_EXPORT __declspec(dllimport)
+#endif
 #else // !__GNUC__
 #ifdef _WIN32
 // PyTorch2 doesn't currently work on Windows. Exporting these APIs can lead
-- 
